/// a double-double from a table and a polynomial, multiplied by `y`, and `2^(y log2(x))` comes
/// from a table of `2^(i/64)` and a polynomial. When the error bound does not decide the
/// rounding, the accurate passes redo it in 128 and then 256 bits, after checking for a result
/// that lies exactly on a rounding boundary.
fn libm_pow(x0 : f64, y0 : f64) -> f64 {
